Z||000000||drednot||06-01-2001||10:36 AM||||I did the conversion on my Dads work (Broad Street cruiser) car.  Just let the little bit of R-12 that it had left in the system out.  Then I changed the fittings and put the new stuff in.  No flushing, no gauges etc.  I just followed the directions on the box.  It still works great.  It has for about 5 months.  The compressor makes a slight wooring sound since I put the new stuff in, But I think it is just because the new stuff is harder to pump.  BTW- My dads work car is a  1992 Pontiac Sunbird 3.1 Manual Transaxle (J-car).  It is actually a quick car.  I just thought I would share about how well it worked for his car.||||reg||6
